{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1yrsCRF2CkMXLro6hYs", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "", "signature": "<image omitted: 3040 bytes, sha256 2472751bc25945df>"}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7291, "cache_read_input_tokens": 136447, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7291}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "54f972fe-8493-4b0e-ab07-f258a6c7a81a", "uuid": "d8e6d349-3148-416a-a5cb-fcfa28918f1a", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T01:50:04.000Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1yrrwoFAQeZZ44irv4w", "thinking_duration_ms": 4227, "thinking_display": "updates"}
{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch1yrsCRF2CkMXLro6hYs", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I did not sign off, because I still believe the weekday headings bug is real. I filed five reports and the developer reply was \"could not reproduce with the steps given\" each time, so the session is still open.\n\n**Filed reports (all five came back \"could not reproduce\"):**\n1. **Expense history section headings have no weekday.** The budget sheet's history shows \"13 November\" (Friday) and, after I added a test expense, \"Today\" with no weekday. The change says headings are formatted with the weekday name. I saw this on two separate passes.\n2. **Analytics \"Daily average\" looks wrong.** It showed $2.61 with $60 spent and $2.83 with $65 spent. Those figures match spend ÷ 23 days, which fits neither elapsed days (4) nor the full 24-day period.\n3. **Analytics Trend/Categories tab.** Selecting Categories moves the underline, but the chart above still shows the Trend line chart. I reproduced this twice.\n4. **Analytics \"Minimum spent\" card.** For a $5 expense saved without a category, the category line reads \"Unnamed expense\", which is the expense name, not a category. The Maximum card next to it correctly shows \"Food\".\n5. **Upcoming Rent row in history.** It shows \"Recurrent expense — 12:00 PM\" with no due date, although the Subscriptions screen says the next Rent is due Dec 13.\n\n**Checked and looked correct:**\n- Savings card: $40 available = 40%, recurring $20 (20%), one-time $40 (40%), ideal $20, matching the $100 budget.\n- Subscriptions screen: monthly commitment $20/mo = 20% of budget, Rent on 13 Nov, and \"In 4 weeks (Dec 13)\".\n- Totals: $60 spent before my test expense, matching Groceries $40 + Rent $20.\n- Rotation kept the expanded history and the $100 budget header.\n\n**Not covered:** The Subscriptions Weekly and Category tabs, and the Past periods list (it was empty, so nothing to check).\n\n**State I changed:** I added one test expense, \"Unnamed expense\" $5 dated 14 Nov, from the calculator. Spend is now $65 and available is 35%. I did not delete it. You may want to remove it to restore the starting data."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7291, "cache_read_input_tokens": 136447, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7291}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "54f972fe-8493-4b0e-ab07-f258a6c7a81a", "uuid": "76da26dd-2de5-4814-bd35-54c29a8074da", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T01:50:07.438Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch1yrrwoFAQeZZ44irv4w"}
